d%29'],
['2013','Design Indaba Music Circuit',"Four days after the album launch, BEAST play the Design Indaba Music Circuit at Aces n Spades as part of a three-day Cape Town programme spanning 32 artists and eight venues.",'https://www.designindaba.com/articles/design-indaba-news/raucous-rock-aces-n-spades'],
['2013','RAMfest',"BEAST are billed for RAMfest Cape Town, 7–10 March at Circle of Dreams near Riviersonderend, on a bill with Rise Against, Bring Me The Horizon and Pendulum.",'https://www.thegremlin.co.za/2013/02/25/sa-bands-have-some-surprises-up-their-sleeves-for-ramfest-2013/'],
['2013','The documentary and international press',"A short documentary follows the album launch, and on 28 August VICE/Noisey premieres the Smoke Swig Swear video alongside an interview with Inge Beckmann and the band's story.",'https://www.vice.com/en/article/premiere-watch-beasts-video-for-smoke-swig-swear/'],
['2013','Line-up change',"Sasha Righini leaves to pursue his own music and Werner von Waltsleben of Kobus! takes over on drums.",'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beast_%28South_African_band%29'],
['2014','Crowdfunding Bardo',"On 13 August BEAST launch an Indiegogo campaign to fund album two while remaining unsigned and protecting their creative independence. A private investor later helps complete the record.",'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beast_%28South_African_band%29'],
['2015','Private Bardo acoustic launch',"On 21 February, backers, family and friends attend an intimate acoustic launch at the Cape Town Club, with the material rearranged for a quieter setting.",'https://lauramccullagh.com/blog/2015/02/beast-bardo-exclusive-acoustic-launch-at-the-cape-town-club/'],
['2015','Bardo launches publicly',"The second album receives its public launch on 27 February. Contemporary listings describe the record as the result of the band's 2014 fan-funded recording push.",'https://www.webtickets.co.za/v2/event.aspx?itemid=1447793371'],
['2015','Splashy Fen',"BEAST are announced for Splashy Fen's 2–6 April Easter-weekend edition near Underberg, joining a broad South African bill including Taxi Violence, Shortstraw, aKING and Nakhane Toure.",'https://www.citizen.co.za/highway-mail/uncategorized/2015/02/24/sas-hottest-acts-to-perform-at-splashy-fen/'],
['2015','Critical peak for Bardo',"On 9 April the Mail & Guardian asks whether BEAST might be South Africa's finest live rock act, praising the force of the two-bass setup and Inge Beckmann's vocal range.",'https://mg.co.za/friday/2015-04-09-could-this-be-sa-s-finest-live-rock-act/']
